  "body": "```\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<script>\ndocument.documentElement.textContent = typeof document.createElement(\"th\").headers;\n</script>\n```\n\nOutputs \"string\" in IE 11 and recent Chrome/Firefox.  Spec says it should be \"object\".  Is there any compelling reason that implementations should change, or should the spec change?\n\n@bzbarsky @annevk\n",
